&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;Logos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A set of logos I&#039;ve made for the various Foundation departments and divisions. Updates pretty frequently, as I like to use these for department or division report backgrounds (as seen &lt;a href=&quot;http://scp-wiki.net/scp-5880&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;). Feel free to use any of them however you like, and let me know if you need a logo for a department or division that doesn&#039;t have one yet!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;wiki-content-table&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Icon&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Inspiration&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/e/2PACX-1vRBze5w1FIDAKKtCckoguQKTCKCW_dzk2Y-hDzP3FZY5Mnn_XJP6WKjG8zfLvHLjQ_Gekca0xKiI_HW/pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; width=&quot;250 px&quot; alt=&quot;pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Administrative Department:&lt;/strong&gt; Triangles are a strong shape. Also, top-down management.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/e/2PACX-1vSEMiHQ6WYZDDQSjsg303342rDKyBVXvnsTy8tMu9rgRrQuqtYKGd4zGD6Gdsm0CXK2g_p8bpFi5J-r/pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; width=&quot;250 px&quot; alt=&quot;pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Occult Studies Division:&lt;/strong&gt; Ouroboros, an ancient symbol associated with magic.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/e/2PACX-1vRcV3QE4ACx_5oCYPtdlM-qYwMCtzWBc0i_hMajioE6e66sxyl0rzLF4imG-YK2QdPT69bWY2UgCaId/pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; width=&quot;250 px&quot; alt=&quot;pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IT Department:&lt;/strong&gt; Modified USB to have three arrows, like the Foundation.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/e/2PACX-1vRO-PpC3s7nCBJ6FbvbJJSgNFInVZSR4GjctJGWyyzYp-Hx-OBYdsCKSWDhMaDOtsX93087jwXMi9Nd/pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; width=&quot;250 px&quot; alt=&quot;pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Memetics and Infohazards Division:&lt;/strong&gt; Negative space. Memes exist &lt;em&gt;inside&lt;/em&gt; of us, so the arrow symbolizes entering our own consciousness.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/e/2PACX-1vTKdNHF4047T3200eXUbGsX83rIzt0GEnSaan7Pqg1_Z7vHCNxNEn6okX1oJ83uzemNZXu22W6CIA58/pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; width=&quot;250 px&quot; alt=&quot;pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Medical Department:&lt;/strong&gt; The Rod of Asclepius, symbolic of the Greek god of healing. Two snakes is the Caduceus, which actually has nothing to do with medicine.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/e/2PACX-1vSf-HTSZyhj8I09TjLe7SnrREUU2VgEmfc7XV9NlmP2gaTuEfT_n2JfO0W9vneBNcYFL5EcJkTz6dVN/pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; width=&quot;250 px&quot; alt=&quot;pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5 Command:&lt;/strong&gt; A scaled-up version of the Administrative Department logo, with three arrowheads added inside. Also, the negative space resembles a V, the Roman numeral for five.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/e/2PACX-1vTkOupqpVLeYOYtj2uKq9xcE-SGgEBuvxTZMLGArXqYKrlfkkCBO-qMw4BokATjxJEAKJNBdFT9MiLt/pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; width=&quot;250 px&quot; alt=&quot;pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethics Committee:&lt;/strong&gt; A scale, the universal symbol for justice, modified to resemble three arrows pointing heavenward, since their duty is above humanity.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/e/2PACX-1vSmPr9Ff3WwgZNcNhueWvdMY9ni19Zt76YORYh6r2HkpZGEniWUw1QmMuvccPGp4q6xu1nbPjwTYbmm/pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; width=&quot;250 px&quot; alt=&quot;pub?w=599&amp;amp;h=600&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decommissioning Department:&lt;/strong&gt; For &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calibri-bold&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5045819&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1606206239&quot; alt=&quot;Calibri Bold&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5045819)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calibri-bold&quot;  &gt;Calibri Bold&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;, even though he didn&#039;t ask. Just a simple symbol universally recognized as meaning no.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;wiki-tab-0-1&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;Icons&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Icons for &lt;a href=&quot;http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/anomaly-classification-system-guide&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;ACS&lt;/a&gt;. For more custom icons, check out &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scp-wiki.net/dr-moned-s-icons-and-art&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Dr Moned&#039;s art page&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;wiki-content-table&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Logo&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Inspiration&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/e/2PACX-1vT9LHefvI_BD_Q4ShhBbOUEV_6SEAeUDFG9WL_ZLd3Nm494EJR7sbm1vZCl3S2heIxAMpX_CVVgkhj3/pub?w=360&amp;amp;h=360&quot; width=&quot;250 px&quot; alt=&quot;pub?w=360&amp;amp;h=360&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zurvan:&lt;/strong&gt; As seen in &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-5103&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;SCP-5103&lt;/a&gt;, by yours truly. Based on the narrative, as well as the traditional depiction of the Zoroastrian god Zurvan.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;http://www.scp-wiki.net/local--files/greyve-art-page/Decommissioned.png&quot; width=&quot;250 px&quot; alt=&quot;Decommissioned.png&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decommissioned:&lt;/strong&gt; Revived by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calibri-bold&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5045819&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1606206239&quot; alt=&quot;Calibri Bold&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5045819)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calibri-bold&quot;  &gt;Calibri Bold&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;. Why did I make my own when he already has one? I like making things complicated for myself.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;wiki-tab-0-2&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;Sketches&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sketches of skips, or whatever else, I guess. Feel free to commission a sketch from me for absolutely no cost, with no satisfaction guarantee!&lt;/p&gt;
