&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;[&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3693&quot;&gt;SCP-3693&lt;/a&gt;] [&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E0EBOFL_VwE&quot;&gt;♬&lt;/a&gt;] &amp;#8212; &lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3693&quot;&gt;Postscript - Through A Glass, Darkly&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (with &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djkaktus&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1888434&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1606206240&quot; alt=&quot;djkaktus&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1888434)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djkaktus&quot;  &gt;djkaktus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;&amp;#32;&amp;#32;&amp;#32;&amp;#32;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;Further investigation of the site discovered an abundance of crushed concrete debris and twisted rebar, as well as several floor drains clogged with blood and fecal matter.&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt; ►&amp;nbsp;Commentary&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt; ▼&amp;nbsp;Close&amp;nbsp;File&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be honest, it feels a little weird to put this one on here; &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djkaktus&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1888434&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1606206240&quot; alt=&quot;djkaktus&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1888434)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djkaktus&quot;  &gt;djkaktus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; came to me with an article he was working on that amounted to &#039;a statue you could put in front of SCP-173 and end its threat forever&#039;, and I gave feedback. I ended up re-arranging the order of a lot of sentences and changing some wording, as well as suggesting some different features. He asked if I wanted collaboration credit, and I said I was cool with him going either way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I like the piece for how it hints at a melancholy story without being overt about it. I suspect that SCP-3693 doesn&#039;t like SCP-173; I also suspect that this feeling is mutual.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;[&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3760&quot;&gt;SCP-3760&lt;/a&gt;] [&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L3wchrctxFo&quot;&gt;♬&lt;/a&gt;] &amp;#8212; &lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3760&quot;&gt;He&#039;s got lifeless eyes. Black eyes. Like a doll&#039;s eyes.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (with &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/peppersghost&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1553042&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1606206240&quot; alt=&quot;PeppersGhost&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1553042)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/peppersghost&quot;  &gt;PeppersGhost&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;&amp;#32;&amp;#32;&amp;#32;&amp;#32;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;These aforementioned orifices will repeatedly seek edible material for consumption; this behavior intensifies in the presence of blood, and may even include acts of autocannibalism.&lt;/em&gt;
